  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(A) The troposphere extends upward to about <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>miles</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>or</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>about</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>33</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>feet</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;above sea level.&nbsp;</p><p>(B)&nbsp;The Electrical-layer or E-part of stratosphere lies&nbsp;approximately <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>&nbsp;over Earth&rsquo;s surface</p><p>(C) The&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>-part of thermosphere lies approximately <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>&nbsp;over Earth&rsquo;s surface.</p><p>(D) D-part of Stratosphere lies approximate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>65</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math><br />&nbsp;over Earth&rsquo;s surface</p><p>Thus,&nbsp;A-III, B-IV, C-II, D-I.</p>",
